cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "MAD: SIFT Malicious Agent Detection"
abstract: >
  MAD is a complete forensic detection stack for AI-driven cyberattacks on
  the SANS SIFT Workstation. It consists of three integrated components:
  MABE (Malicious Agent Behavior Emulator), a synthetic dataset generator
  producing labeled Windows Security Event and Sysmon logs that emulate
  autonomous AI-driven network attacks; MABE Detector, a three-mechanism
  unsupervised behavioral detection system (velocity, enumeration, privilege
  escalation chaining) validated at 100% precision and recall against a
  1,425-session dataset; and an agentic investigation layer built on
  Claude Code and a custom MCP server that autonomously investigates flagged
  sessions using Protocol SIFT tools and produces CISO-readable forensic reports.
